## Anatomy of an Interface

```xiom
pub interface Comparable[T] {
  fn compare(self: &T, other: &T) -> Ordering;
  fn less_than(self: &T, other: &T) -> Bool;
  fn greater_than(self: &T, other: &T) -> Bool;
}
```

### Interface Design Principles

1. **Single Responsibility**: Each interface should do ONE thing
2. **Minimal Methods**: Fewer methods = easier to implement
3. **Clear Semantics**: Names should communicate intent

### Self Parameter Convention
```xiom
pub interface Processor {
  // &Self — immutable reference, can read but not modify
  fn inspect(self: &Self) -> Str;

  // &mut Self — mutable reference, can modify
  fn process(self: &mut Self, input: Str) -> Str;

  // Self — takes ownership
  fn consume(self: Self) -> Str;
}
```

### Interface with Associated Functions
```xiom
pub interface FromStr[T] {
  fn from_str(s: Str) -> Result[T, ParseError];  // No self — static method
}
```

### Real-World Interface Design
```xiom
pub interface Validator[T] {
  fn validate(self: &T) -> Result<(), Vec[Str]>;
}

pub interface Serializer[T] {
  fn serialize(self: &T) -> Str;
}

pub interface Deserializer[T] {
  fn deserialize(s: Str) -> Result[T, ParseError];
}
```

